    "summary_one_sentence": "Convinced that the tragic death of her patient was actually a murder, renowned Paris psychiatrist Lilian Steiner launches her own private investigation to uncover the truth.",
    "summary_short": "When her longtime patient Paula is found dead in an apparent suicide, renowned Parisian psychiatrist Lilian Steiner refuses to accept the official report. Suspecting foul play, Lilian begins a personal investigation that pushes her far beyond her professional boundaries. With the help of her ex-husband and a hypnotist whose sessions unleash unsettling visions, Lilian navigates a maze of suspicion and buried secrets. Her relentless search for answers gradually blurs the lines between intuition, memory, and obsession.",
    "summary_long": "Renowned Paris-based psychiatrist Lilian Steiner is shaken to her core when her patient Paula Cohen-Solal is found dead, a death quickly ruled a suicide by authorities. Refusing to accept this official explanation, Lilian grows convinced that Paula was murdered, focusing her initial suspicions on the victim's husband. Driven by a deep sense of responsibility and growing obsession, Lilian steps past her professional boundaries to launch an independent investigation. To help navigate the emerging mystery, she enlists the assistance of her ex-husband as she digs into Paula's family and personal history. Seeking deeper insights, Lilian visits a hypnotist, triggering vivid visions that suggest a complex web of shared history, memory, and unseen connections. As she probes deeper into the enigmatic circumstances surrounding the demise, Lilian finds herself tangled in a maze where personal trauma and professional duty collide. Her unconventional sleuthing leads to surprising revelations about both the people around her and her own inner life. Suspense builds as Lilian balances dark humor, complex personal relationships, and escalating psychological tension. Ultimately, Lilian's investigation becomes an intense journey through memory, grief, and truth, challenging everything she thought she knew about her patient and herself.",
    "synopsis": "Directed by Rebecca Zlotowski, *A Private Life* (*Vie privée*) follows Dr. Lilian Steiner, a respected psychiatrist practicing in Paris, whose world is upended when her patient Paula dies under mysterious circumstances. Though authorities conclude Paula committed suicide, Lilian is firmly convinced that her patient was murdered. Stepping out from behind the therapeutic desk, Lilian embarks on an unofficial investigation that entangles her with Paula's family and her own past. Aided by her ex-husband Gabriel and influenced by hypnotic sessions that conjure strange visions, Lilian plunges into a stylish blend of Hitchcockian suspense, psychological tension, and subtle dark comedy. *A Private Life* is a compelling, spoiler-free exploration of grief, intuition, memory, and the hidden depths of human psychology.",
